{"id":113013246089124,"type":"artist","name":"Oranssi Pazuzu","artist":null,"year":2007,"weight":10,"info":{"bio":"Oranssi Pazuzu es una banda finlandesa activa desde el año 2007. Proponen un mix de black metal con psicodelia y kraut atmosférico que ocupa las esquinas más oscuras del espacio y la mente. Entre sus influencias podemos contar a  Burzum, Electric Wizard y Pink Floyd.\n\nEn definitiva Oranssi Pazuzu hace una música que invita a todos los piromaníacos y a los fumones a tomarse de las manos y mirar las estrellas. . User-contributed text is available under the Creative Commons By-SA License; additional terms may apply.","tags":["black metal","psychedelic black metal","experimental","psychedelic","finnish"],"country":"FI","origin":"Finland","begin":"2007","kind":"Group","aliases":"Waste of Space Orchestra,Imperial Triumphant,Deathspell Omega,Blut aus Nord,Doedsmaghird","member_of":"black metal,psychedelic black metal,experimental,psychedelic,finnish","similar":["Waste of Space Orchestra","Imperial Triumphant","Krallice","Blut aus Nord","Deathspell Omega","Aluk Todolo","Dødheimsgard","Hail Spirit Noir","Schammasch","Havukruunu"],"wikipedia":"Oranssi Pazuzu is a Finnish psychedelic black metal band formed in 2007. The band originally consisted of vocalist and guitarist Juho \"Jun-His\" Vanhanen, drummer Jarkko \"Korjak\" Salo, guitarist Moit, keyboardist and percussionist Ville \"Evil\" Leppilahti, and bassist Toni \"Ontto\" Hietamäki. Moit left the band in 2016 and was replaced by Niko \"Ikon\" Lehdontie of Kairon; IRSE!.\n\nThe band takes its name from \"oranssi\", the Finnish word for the color orange, and Pazuzu, a wind demon from Babylonian mythology.[3]\n\nThe band recorded their debut album, Muukalainen puhuu in 2008 in Korjak's family cabin. It was released via Violent Journey Records in 2009 and followed in 2010 by a split LP with Candy Cane. Their second full-length album, Kosmonument, was released in 2011 through Spinefarm. In 2013, Svart issued the follow-up, Valonielu which was produced and engineered by London-based producer Jaime Gomez Arellano. The band's album Värähtelijä was released in 2016[3] and received positive reviews from music outlets such as AllMusic,[4] Pitchfork[5] and Spin.[6] Lehdontie, of fellow Finnish band Kairon; IRSE!, joined Oranssi Pazuzu in 2016 first as a live member and later on as a full-time member.[7][8] In 2017, the band released the two-track EP Kevät / Värimyrsky.[9] The band released their fifth album Mestarin kynsi in 2020.\n\nAllMusic's James Christopher Monger described the band's music as a combination of black metal, psychedelic rock, space rock, and progressive metal.[3]\n\nTwo members of Oranssi Pazuzu and two members of Dark Buddha Rising have formed the band Atomikylä. Oranssi Pazuzu is also part of the Wastement collective.[10]\n\nStudio albums\n\nEPs\n\nSplits\n\nCompilations","disambiguation":"Finnish black metal","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/3XFQRe2FsSOjrODygK4caW","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC93Nnu8LP94kTGj3ltMsa3Q","discogs":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/1552158","bandcamp":"https://oranssipazuzu.bandcamp.com","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/artist/oranssi-pazuzu","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oranssi_Pazuzu","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/e9d2cdf6-d485-4074-9a53-9990c9a4d8b1"},"img":null},"works":[{"id":199850431143485,"type":"album","name":"Kosmonument","artist":"Oranssi Pazuzu","year":2011,"weight":7,"yt":"0_bt9uO4K90","src":"charts,musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":155836457058310,"name":"Scaruffi 2010s","rank":280,"scaruffi":7.0}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":3891018998524,"type":"album","name":"Varahtelija","artist":"Oranssi Pazuzu","year":2016,"weight":11,"yt":"qTFSZ6h4BZA","src":"charts,musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":50051288032588,"name":"Sputnikmusic Best Albums 2016","rank":187,"scaruffi":7.0},{"id":155836457058310,"name":"Scaru